this runs aslp on a list of opcodes derived from the cntlm binary (specifically, cntlm-new.adt).
the aslt format is displayed first. below that, antlr is run and if successful, should produce no error output.

  $ java -jar ./antlr.jar ./Semantics.g4

  $ javac -cp ./antlr.jar *.java

  $ echo ':set +dis:check_rasl' > commands
  $ for op in $(grep '^0x' ./cntlm-ops.txt); do printf '%s\n' "\"$op\"" ":ast A64 $op"; done >> commands

  $ asli < commands > stmts

strip opcode information before passing to antlr.

  $ grep -v '^"' stmts > stmts_raw
 
